Adds explicit regime breakpoints in app/config.py::REGIMES with four regimes:

  pre_redenom      2001-01-01 -> 2013-01-01   Pre-redenomination (ZMK)
  pre_default      2013-01-01 -> 2020-11-13   Pre-Eurobond default
  default_no_imf   2020-11-13 -> 2022-08-31   Eurobond default, no IMF programme
  imf_ecf          2022-08-31 -> today         IMF Extended Credit Facility

Each regime carries a one-sentence narrative explaining the macro anchor.

Two new pieces of API surface:

  GET /api/regimes       -> the regime list (start, end, key, label, narrative)
  GET /api/events        -> now tags each event with regime + regime_label

The regime_for(date) helper in config.py does the date-window lookup. The UI
can now draw vertical bands at the breakpoints and colour-code events by regime.

The scenario module's existing empirical regime-sensitivity detector (recent
vs full-history betas) continues to run alongside these explicit breakpoints.

75 tests passing (1 new).
